Personally I prefer to use them to convert myself to lawful,
given that I find a lawful altar early enough in the game.
[100% chance of converting if you do it right]
You can sacrifice immediately (given suitable candidates) to
undo the retribution of your old deity, and thereafter you
can turn all the altars you meet into lawful ones.

Better still is a helm of opposite alignment.  If I am neutral
I put it on to be chaotic, sacrifice a human on an altar: 100%
chance of converting the altar to chaotic, which results in +2
luck (as far as I remember: +1 for the altar-convertion, +1
for the human sacrifice). Then use the helmet to become lawful,
and convert the altar back again  (chance of losing luck - but
on the whole you gain luck) - repeat as neccessary until you
run out of humans (shopkeepers, soldiers, nurses, [kops?], ...)
- best helmet there is, with only the minor inconvenience that
it normally starts cursed.

Noone seems to have mentioned character-convertion on here before
that I can remember - am I the only one who does it or have I not
been paying attention ?

